      "ts": "20260831_1408",
      "sender_norm": "POLITICO",
      "subject": "China shows its IMO hand",
      "pdf": "data/pdfs/20260831_1408_China_shows_its_IMO_hand.pdf",
      "date_label": "AUG 31  14:08",
      "read_min": 9,
      "toyota": true,
      "excerpt": "中国がIMOの脱炭素化枠組みに関する具体的な提案を提示し、両派の間で妥協点を模索する柔軟な",
      "subject_en": "China shows its IMO hand",
      "html": "data/pdfs/20260831_1408_China_shows_its_IMO_hand.html",
      "summary_en": "China has proposed changes to the IMO's contested Net-Zero Framework for shipping decarbonization, urging flexibility to bridge the divide between the EU, which backs the current framework, and the US, Saudi Arabia, and other nations pushing for major revisions. The move comes as climate negotiations resume this week, with Beijing avoiding a clear alignment with either side. Meanwhile, EU lawmakers remain split on 2035 emissions targets for automakers, and Germany plans to add local content rules to its EV incentive program.",
      "summary_ja": "中国はIMOの海運脱炭素化に関する「ネットゼロ枠組み」について、具体的な修正案を提示し、これを支持するEUと、大幅な見直しを求める米国・サウジアラビアなどの対立を調整する柔軟性を求めた。今週再開する気候交渉を前に、北京はどちらの陣営にも明確に与しない姿勢を示している。一方、EU議会では2035年の自動車排出目標を巡り意見が割れており、ドイツはEV補助制度に現地調達要件を追加する方針だ。",
      "summary_pdf": ""
