  "toyota_summary_en": "EU lawmakers remain divided on 2035 emissions targets for automakers, leaving manufacturers without clarity on long-term compliance planning. This uncertainty complicates investment decisions across the bloc's auto sector.\n\nGermany plans to attach local content rules to its EV incentive program, potentially reshaping supply chain strategies for automakers selling into the German market. Companies reliant on imported components may face new cost pressures.\n\nIMO shipping decarbonization talks are provided for reference."
